    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The BASIC computer program KWM computes the parameters of the kinematic wave model for debris flows proposed by Arattano and Savage (1992) using the hydrographs recorded by two gaging stations along a channel. The model also can be used to predict the movement along a stream channel of a known mass of debris caused by a landslide or a previous debris flow. If debris volume, the amount of water required for obilization and the mean width of the stream channel are known, the parameters H, maximum height of the initial debris mass, and L, length of the initial debris mass, can be calculated. If we then have a value for k, a parameter that accounts for changes of hydraulic radius with flow depth, and for C, the roughness coefficient, along the stream channel, the propagation of the debris flow can be\r\npredicted (Arattano and Savage, 1992).\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
